cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use AiEDs, cite the methodology version you implemented."
title: "AiEDs - AI Energy Disclosure Standard"
# CFF 1.2.0 allows only 'dataset' or 'software' here. This work is a
# standard, but that is not an option the format offers at the top level,
# and an invalid file makes GitHub drop the citation panel entirely.
type: software
version: 2.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-12
license: CC-BY-4.0
license-url: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
repository-code: https://github.com/random-knights/standard
url: https://standard.rand0m.ai
abstract: >-
  An open schema and toolset for self-attested energy and carbon footprint
  disclosures for AI models, agents, and apps. Energy is modeled first from
  per-model coefficients; carbon is derived from energy. Scope is device,
  usage, inference, and training. It is not a planetary health score.
keywords:
  - AI energy disclosure
  - carbon accounting
  - inference energy
  - open standard
authors:
  - name: "Random Knights, LLC"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-5066-1693"
    city: Roswell
    region: Georgia
    country: US
    website: https://randomknights.xyz
contact:
  - name: "Random Knights, LLC"
    email: knights@rand0m.ai
# K13 - AI Response Standard lives in this same repository (K13.md) and has
# its own citation file, CITATION.k13.cff. A CFF file describes one work, so
# the two standards are not folded into one entry here.
